---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BarkField from '../components/BarkField.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About · Birch Design Lab"
  description="The name, the oldest paper of the north, and the person behind Birch Design Lab."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="intro">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <!-- provisional copy throughout -->
    <article class="epic" data-reveal>
      <p class="etym">
        <em>Birch</em>: Old English <em>beorc</em>, from an ancient root that
        meant <strong>to shine</strong>. The same syllable survives in
        <em>bright</em>. The birch is, quite literally, the shining tree,
        named for the way its white bark stands out in a dark wood.
      </p>
      <p>
        The word is old enough to have kept its own letter. When English was
        still written in runes, the rune for B was called <em>beorc</em>: the
        birch rune. A tree so familiar it stood for a sound. Most business
        names get invented in an afternoon. This one has been earning its
        keep for a few thousand years.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="myth" data-reveal>
      <h2>The oldest paper of the north</h2>
      <p>
        Birch bark is the oldest paper of the north. The medieval letters dug
        out of Novgorod's mud (shopping lists, love notes, a child's
        homework) were scratched into bark and survived eight hundred years.
        The shining tree is also the tree you could write on: the original
        carrier of everyday people's messages.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a business that builds the surfaces where companies speak to the
        world, that is not just decoration. That is the entire job
        description.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="founder" data-reveal>
      <h2>The founder</h2>
      <p>
        Birch Design Lab is one person, a builder of websites and software
        who happens to resemble the namesake: tall, pale, and better suited
        to the north than to the Gulf Coast he currently calls home. Every
        project here is designed, constructed, and cared for by the same
        pair of hands you shake.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="field-strip" data-reveal>
      <BarkField density={90} />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro { padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-4); }
  .epic, .myth, .founder { padding-block: var(--space-5); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); max-width: 60ch; }
  .etym { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); line-height: 1.4; }
  .epic p + p, .myth p, .founder p { color: var(--mark-muted); margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .field-strip {
    position: relative; margin-block: var(--space-6);
    min-height: 14rem;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line); overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>
